## Security Guidelines

### Django Security

- Apply Django's security best practices (CSRF protection, SQL injection protection, XSS prevention)
- Use HTTPS in production environments
- Implement proper session security
- Configure security headers appropriately

### API Security

- Implement JWT token authentication with proper expiration
- Use HTTPS for all API communications
- Implement rate limiting for API endpoints
- Validate all API inputs and sanitize outputs
- Use proper HTTP status codes for security responses

### WebSocket Security

- Implement WebSocket authentication
- Validate WebSocket message content
- Handle WebSocket connection security
- Implement proper access controls for WebSocket channels

### Database Security

- Use parameterized queries (Django ORM handles this)
- Implement proper database user permissions
- Use environment variables for database credentials
- Implement database connection encryption

### File Upload Security

- Validate file uploads (type, size, content)
- Store uploaded files securely
- Implement virus scanning for uploaded files
- Use secure file serving methods

### Authentication & Authorization

- Implement proper user authentication
- Use role-based access control
- Implement proper password policies
- Handle user session management securely
